From 4e77190ec326b5dc0eabae09218b33dfcbc1b9a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bench <bench@local>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 02:32:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 26/75] perf(field_t): compile-time Montgomery 1 and -1

bb::fr::one() / bb::fr::neg_one() convert to Montgomery form at runtime outside constant expressions (the
x86 Montgomery multiplication is inline asm), so every field_t constructor and every is_normalized() call paid
a field multiplication. field_t::ONE / NEG_ONE are static constexpr and hold the same values.
---
 .../stdlib/primitives/field/field.cpp         | 52 +++++++++----------
 .../stdlib/primitives/field/field.hpp         | 23 ++++----
 2 files changed, 40 insertions(+), 35 deletions(-)

